      "writtenOn": "2026-11-02T20:08:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK, so I\u0027ve looked at everything more carefully...\n\nThe \"user.\" prefix is not supposed to be on the wire despite pynfs using it.\n\nFSAL_VFS, FSAL_GLUSTER, and FSAL_CEPH all add \"user.\" prefix on set/get/remove and use the helper function to filter on \"user.\" and remove it for listxattr.\n\nSo FSAL_GPFS has to be modified to add \"user.\" prefix in set/get/remove.\n\nNote that with this, the actual xattr set by pynfs will be user.user.xattr1 for example. This is odd but should be OK, and pynfs is the only code that ever looks at the xattrs it sets.",
      "revId": "57803190130272a2267a48df8062e0ff444d0985",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    }
